# govulncheck has no native suppression mechanism, so this file is one. `make vuln` fails on a
# vulnerability govulncheck reports as reachable from messq's own code, unless a live entry
# here names it.
#
# Every field is mandatory. The expiry is the last day the entry is honoured; past it the build
# fails whether or not the vulnerability is still reported, so a suppression rots loudly instead
# of becoming a list nobody reads. The reason names the issue that removes it.
#
# An empty file is the expected steady state.
#
# osv-id         expires      reason
